# 2026-07-12

## Run (easy — bonus, pre-block)
2.02 mi in 21:56 (10:51 avg) — avg HR 157; body of run 155–160, final ~0.25 mi kicked to ~8:30 pace, HR peaked 172

---

First deliberately capped easy run on record. Backing out the kick: ~1.77 mi @ ~11:10/mi under the ceiling → **baseline easy pace ≈ 11:10/mi at ~156 HR** — the block's week-over-week fitness readout starts here.

Audit: avg 157 ≤ 160 → **pass**, but only because the run was short — the closing kick (2 min above threshold, 172 peak) is exactly the effort-creep pattern Run E exists to break. Strides arrive wk 3: 20 seconds, not two minutes. Cutting the kick next time = correct read, not lost fitness.

Sizing was right: third run in 6 days, kept to ~22 min the day after a steady 33-min run. Back-to-back run days closed out the pre-block week; wk 1 opens with a lift day, not a run.
